of had two different takeaways as a result.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.250
And I just worry when I look at, you know,
the Chip Roy's in the Mac gates as if they

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:32.080
even really understand the implications of
the brinkmanship they're practicing and what

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.600
would actually occur if the United States
was to default.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.970
I think that makes I wonder if that makes
the risk so much significantly higher than

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.380
very typically would assume it would be.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.670
Speaker 1: Well, they don't understand it.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.670
But here's the thing.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.080
Even if they did, they wouldn't really care.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.140
So it's one of those things where you're completely
right.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.510
